","closed_at":"2026-08-19T17:22:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 4 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1062) - AMD Ryzen 7 9700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.16 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen you **open a Scene when you have no Scenes opened in the Editor yet, the top node in the Scene Tree is not automatically selected**, which leaves the Inspector completely blank. This leads to having to switch to the Scene Tree, and manually selecting the top node to get access to exported variables etc.\n\n<img width=\"511\" height=\"300\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5b60b242-fad2-434f-9823-0a7d9febdf6e\" />\n\n<img width=\"511\" height=\"300\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e1006255-719f-44cb-8e3f-211aafd3d081\" />\n\n_The top, without a previously opened scene, leads to nothing visible in the Inspector. The normal behaviour, if you have a previously opened scene, is shown in the bottom, where a node is selected after opening the scene._\n\nThere is little reason to not select at least *a* node in the Scene Tree. Many editor docks rely on a selection, so selecting something is better than selecting nothing.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Close all currently opened Scenes in the Editor\n2. Open a scene through the File System\n3. The Inspector will remain blank, since no node in the SceneTree was selected when you opened the scene.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo",